  "description": "NDIPRX10 crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C51 H119 Cl1 Nd6 O17. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.803-4.239 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.23-128.32°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Nd6[OCH(CH3)2]17Cl.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
